            "Here's an in-depth look at endogenous variables:",
            "1. Definition and Identification: An endogenous variable is one whose value is determined within the model. For example, in a supply and demand model, the price and quantity of a good are endogenous because they are determined by the intersection of the supply and demand curves.",
            "2. Interdependence with Other Variables: Endogenous variables often depend on other variables within the model, which can also be endogenous. For instance, investment might depend on interest rates, which in turn depend on monetary policy, an endogenous variable in a macroeconomic model.",
