            "Examples can help illustrate these points. Take, for instance, the relationship between education and earnings. If we simply regress earnings on education, we might find a positive relationship. However, this relationship could be confounded by innate ability\u00e2\u0080\u0094people with higher earnings might also be more likely to obtain more education, not necessarily because education causes higher earnings, but because those with higher ability levels choose to pursue more education. In this case, ability is the omitted variable that leads to endogeneity.",
            "Another example is the relationship between crime rates and police presence. One might think that more police would lead to lower crime rates, but if police are deployed based on crime rates, then the causality could be reversed, leading to simultaneity.",
